#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""vpsmon: health snapshot and one-click cleanup for a Linux server.

The VPS Monitor Mac app runs `/usr/local/bin/vpsmon --lang <en|es> <command>` over ssh and reads one JSON object
from stdout. vpsmon needs root and re-runs itself through `sudo -n` when it is not. docs/contract.md is the contract.

Usage: vpsmon [--lang en|es] status | sample | scan [--background] | act <id> [--dry-run] | uninstall | version

Testing hook: with VPSMON_PREFIX set, vpsmon's own files (state, audit log, config, script, units, sudoers rule) live
under that prefix, and it runs as whoever starts it, without sudo. What it watches (/proc, /tmp, homes) stays real.
"""

